  "ingredients": [
    "1.5 cups wheat bran",
    "1 cup buttermilk",
    "0.66666668653488 cup brown sugar",
    "0.33333334326744 cup vegetable oil",
    "1 egg",
    "0.5 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1 cup all-purpose flour",
    "1 teaspoon baking soda",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "0.5 teaspoon salt",
    "0.5 cup raisins"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/KdAjgLlNyXk3U-iodWP5Rz0SVPM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/25224-classic-bran-muffins-step1-3x4-0135064414801638-52a8b77c987f4fc3882a4dd8825d96b0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/25224/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Grease 12 muffin cups or line with paper muffin liners.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix wheat bran and buttermilk together in a large bowl; let stand for 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/3EA7z-eXh-Vb-pboOzLWhyl0Vk8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/25224-classic-bran-muffins-step2-3x4-0135064414801640-c5946d32aae54a67b85a66aa50926e8d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/25224/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, beat brown sugar, oil, egg, and vanilla together in a separate bowl until light and fluffy; stir into buttermilk mixture.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/eeV6iv4ujzQmg-07RTTn3VPIKEs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/25224-classic-bran-muffins-step4-1-3x4-0135064414801644-bbe98c70968b4d5b8fd5dbcc3a239ab8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/25224/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sift flour, baking soda, baking powder, and salt together; stir into buttermilk mixture until just blended. Fold in raisins; spoon batter into the prepared muffin cups, filling each 2/3 full.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/uVtIMIWqkVr0K2NZTV0_4BmkRO8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/25224-classic-bran-muffins-step6-3x4-0135064414801648-6812d1efecbf4734bf60bc6f08b4e6aa.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/25224/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until tops spring back when lightly pressed, about 15 to 20 minutes. Cool in the tin briefly, then transfer to a wire rack to cool completely. Enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/avBWWY1aXOZn0dE2-Kg142ABzaU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/25224-classic-bran-muffins-beauty-3x4-0135064414801650-cf29039a560b44bb84ee93fad7b618dc.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/25224/step_06.webp"
    }
  ],
